{
  "$data": {
    "description": "Reusable contracts for observed Command Hub facts supplied by the harness rather than authored into a version.",
    "contracts": {
      "pull-request": {
        "description": "One observed pull request, including its Markdown author description, revision, diff statistics, and checks.",
        "instructions": {
          "producer": "Replace the complete source whenever the pull request or its checks change:\n\n```bash\nleaf data set \"$PAGE\" <source-id> --file pull-request.json\n```\n\nThe JSON object carries `repository`, positive integer `number`, `title`, `author`, `base`, `head`, `revision`, `status`, a Markdown `description`, RFC 3339 `observedAt`, a `diff` object counting the change's `files`, `additions`, `deletions`, and `commits`, and a `checks` map from check name to status. Keep the source id on the same pull request for the page's lifetime. Leaf presents these supplied facts; it does not query a forge."
        },
        "schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "repository": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1
            },
            "number": {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 1
            },
            "title": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1
            },
            "author": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1
            },
            "base": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1
            },
            "head": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1
            },
            "revision": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1
            },
            "status": {
              "enum": [
                "draft",
                "open",
                "merged",
                "closed"
              ]
            },
            "description": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "The author's pull-request description as Markdown. Raw HTML is displayed as text."
            },
            "observedAt": {
              "type": "string",
              "format": "date-time"
            },
            "diff": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "files": {
                  "type": "integer",
                  "minimum": 0
                },
                "additions": {
                  "type": "integer",
                  "minimum": 0
                },
                "deletions": {
                  "type": "integer",
                  "minimum": 0
                },
                "commits": {
                  "type": "integer",
                  "minimum": 0
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "files",
                "additions",
                "deletions",
                "commits"
              ],
              "additionalProperties": false
            },
            "checks": {
              "type": "object",
              "propertyNames": {
                "minLength": 1
              },
              "additionalProperties": {
                "enum": [
                  "queued",
                  "running",
                  "passed",
                  "failed",
                  "cancelled",
                  "skipped"
                ]
              }
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "repository",
            "number",
            "title",
            "author",
            "base",
            "head",
            "revision",
            "status",
            "description",
            "observedAt",
            "diff",
            "checks"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": false
        }
      },
      "atlas-worktrees": {
        "description": "Current worktree evidence keyed by the id of its authored lf-atlas-tree seat.",
        "instructions": {
          "coordinator": "After worktree evidence changes, replace the complete page-bound source snapshot rather than republishing it as prose or appending an event:\n\n```bash\nleaf data set \"$PAGE\" <source-id> --file worktrees.json\n```\n\nRead `data_bindings` from `leaf page state \"$PAGE\"` to find source ids using the `atlas-worktrees` contract and their consuming widget ids. `worktrees.json` is an object keyed by authored worktree widget id. Each value carries `branch`, `base`, `head`, non-negative `ahead`, `behind`, `additions`, `deletions`, and `commits`, a `tests` value of `passing`, `failing`, `running`, or `not-run`, an RFC 3339 `observedAt` timestamp with a timezone, and optional `files` and `diff` strings. Keep a key stable for the same worktree, and give a different worktree a new authored lf-atlas-tree id; a reused id would attach old comments to the wrong worktree. Gather these facts with harness tools; Leaf validates, transports, and presents them but does not run git or inspect worker directories."
        },
        "schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "propertyNames": {
            "pattern": "^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$"
          },
          "additionalProperties": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "branch": {
                "type": "string",
                "minLength": 1
              },
              "base": {
                "type": "string",
                "minLength": 1
              },
              "head": {
                "type": "string",
                "minLength": 1
              },
              "ahead": {
                "type": "integer",
                "minimum": 0
              },
              "behind": {
                "type": "integer",
                "minimum": 0
              },
              "additions": {
                "type": "integer",
                "minimum": 0
              },
              "deletions": {
                "type": "integer",
                "minimum": 0
              },
              "commits": {
                "type": "integer",
                "minimum": 0
              },
              "tests": {
                "enum": [
                  "passing",
                  "failing",
                  "running",
                  "not-run"
                ]
              },
              "observedAt": {
                "type": "string",
                "format": "date-time"
              },
              "files": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "diff": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "branch",
              "base",
              "head",
              "ahead",
              "behind",
              "additions",
              "deletions",
              "commits",
              "tests",
              "observedAt"
            ],
            "additionalProperties": false
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "lf-pr-brief": {
    "description": "The review packet’s live author brief and observed checks.",
    "x-instructions": "Place one empty element before the agent-authored walkthrough and bind it to the page's pull-request source. The widget labels the original author description, so surrounding prose can carry the reviewer's analysis.",
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "id": {
        "type": "string",
        "pattern": "^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$"
      },
      "source": {
        "type": "string",
        "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$"
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "id",
      "source"
    ],
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "x-content": "empty",
    "x-data": {
      "request": {
        "contract": "pull-request",
        "source": "source"
      }
    },
    "x-upgrade": true,
    "x-height": true
  },
  "lf-merge-film": {
    "description": "An animated, scrubbable film of worktrunk's wt merge, drawn as one SVG in the page's colours, with flags that re-plot the run. Its commits, refs, worktrees and hook chips are commentable visual parts while they are on screen. Each paint dispatches a bubbling film-frame event naming the current step, its caption and the run's status per step.",
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "id": {
        "type": "string",
        "pattern": "^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$"
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "id"
    ],
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "x-content": "empty",
    "x-upgrade": true,
    "x-visual": {
      "prefixes": [
        "commit:",
        "ref:",
        "tree:",
        "hook:"
      ]
    },
    "x-space": "available"
  },
  "lf-merge-steps": {
    "description": "The steps of a merge film, told beside it. Its content is one authored <ol>: an <li data-chapter> per step, each with an <h3> title, a <p> saying what the step does, and an empty <p class=\"this-run\">. The module marks the step playing, how this run treats each step, and fills this-run with why a step was skipped or stopped; a click on a step holds its result in the film named by `for` for reading.",
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "id": {
        "type": "string",
        "pattern": "^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$"
      },
      "for": {
        "type": "string",
        "pattern": "^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$"
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "id",
      "for"
    ],
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "x-content": "markup",
    "x-refers": {
      "for": {}
    },
    "x-upgrade": true
  },
  "lf-sort-film": {
    "description": "An animated, scrubbable trace of the merge sort Rust shipped in 1.15, drawn as one SVG in the page's palette: the slice, the scratch buffer, and the run stack with its collapse() checks. It indicates the source line each step executes in the lf-code excerpts its sort-code, head-code and merge-code attributes name, by the line's number in slice.rs. The current step, each slot of the slice, the scratch lane, the run stack and each collapse() clause are commentable visual parts.",
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "id": {
        "type": "string",
        "pattern": "^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$"
      },
      "sort-code": {
        "type": "string",
        "pattern": "^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$"
      },
      "head-code": {
        "type": "string",
        "pattern": "^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$"
      },
      "merge-code": {
        "type": "string",
        "pattern": "^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$"
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "id"
    ],
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "x-content": "empty",
    "x-upgrade": true,
    "x-space": "wide",
    "x-visual": {
      "prefixes": [
        "v:",
        "lane:",
        "stack:",
        "check:",
        "moment:"
      ]
    },
    "x-refers": {
      "sort-code": {},
      "head-code": {},
      "merge-code": {}
    }
  },
  "$work": {
    "description": "Atlas work roles read through the public work projection.",
    "widgets": {
      "lf-atlas-plan": {
        "role": "scope"
      },
      "lf-atlas-task": {
        "role": "goal",
        "state": "status",
        "done": [
          "done"
        ],
        "stopped": [
          "blocked",
          "review",
          "stalled"
        ],
        "review": [
          "review"
        ],
        "stalled": [
          "stalled"
        ],
        "depends": "needs",
        "stoppedAt": "stopped-at"
      },
      "lf-atlas-worker": {
        "role": "worker",
        "state": "state",
        "running": [
          "working"
        ],
        "retired": [
          "reaped",
          "done"
        ],
        "on": "on"
      },
      "lf-atlas-tree": {
        "role": "evidence"
      }
    }
  },
